  "details": "With the addition to security being implemented with EAC, I would like to see better in-game reporting functions to give the power to the players to police any future hackers that bypass EAC. \nI am anticipating future hacking and client use to be more obvious as EAC will ween out the lazy and the less technologically capable from using malicious attacks. Therefor I can see a case where someone would have bypassed EAC and would be using their software maliciously, which would be much more obvious now.\nI would like the added ability to screen capture using the in game camera like we can with invites for evidence. This can be useful for any sexual harassment, avatar, or hateful actions (such as drawings with a pen) reporting as well.\nFurther more, we don't have any reporting functions for reporting suspicious behavior such as modding or exploting. these functions exist in avatar, but most people would not assume that as most malicious attacks I've witnessed are client based attacks that target udon scripts in world.\n\nThis small addition should aid in the VRChats moderation team in identifying future abusers of exploits now that there is potentially less. \"my game is broken because of a mod I am running\" reports.",
